 whom you probably wouldn’t have connected with otherwise.”\\nDr Inge Govaerts, Young National Society Ambassador for Belgium\\nUZ Leuven, Belgium\\n“EHA offers the potential to be part of a community that is broader than a national society, which offers great opportunities to meet colleagues from different countries at events like the Congress.”\\nProf Anne Angelillo-Scherrer, Community Stakeholder Committee Member\\nUniversity of Bern, Switzerland\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-231b33a27177c62cf687d4bb\", \"title\": \"Hemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Hemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3986, \"end\": 4028, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 42}, {\"start\": 4123, \"end\": 4180, \"excerpt_start\": 43, \"excerpt_end\": 100}, {\"start\": 4293, \"end\": 5794, \"excerpt_start\": 101, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Hemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\\nLeft Sidebar\\n3 min read · May 16, 2025\\nMay 16, 2025\\nShare\\nThis program aims to expand awareness and education about increasingly common genetic diseases in Europe among healthcare professionals, patients, and the general population.\\nThe program addresses medical and public health issues in the prevention, early diagnosis, and management of hemoglobinopathies, with a focus on sickle cell disease and beta-thalassemia.\\nEHA’s initiatives\\nSome of the content below is restricted to EHA members. To find out more about joining Europe’s biggest hematology community, either as a member or a guest, visit our membership page.\\nSickle cell disease courses\\nTo access these items, you must be an EHA member.\\nPathophysiology – cell\\nPathophysiology – vessel\\nPathophysiology – tissue\\nEpidemiology & Public Health\\nScreening and Diagnosis\\nComplications\\nTreatment\\nGene Therapy\\nHematology Updates – Sickle Cell Disease\\nThalassemia courses\\nTo access these items, you must be an EHA member.\\nFundamentals\\nMorbidities\\nFamily Planning and QoL\\nTreatment\\nGene Therapy\\nFollow the Iron\\nHematology Updates β-thalassemia\\nEducation programs\\nTo access these items, you must be an EHA member.\\nPodcasts\\nSCD in pregnancy\\nInterventions in Adolescent SCD\\nSocial Stigma and SCD\\nPerspectives in SCD – 1\\nPerspectives in SCD – 2\\nPerspectives in SCD – 3\\nVideos\\nPrecision Medicine and hemoglobinopathies\\nNew Agents for the Treatment of Thalassemia\\nTIF Guidelines for transfusion-dependent Thalassemia\\nClinical cases\\nβ-thalassemia (Myra)\\nResearch\\nSpecialized Working Group on Red Cells and Iron\\nTopi\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-6f5b02f93bee7af3c5bb4d0c\", \"title\": \"Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3994, \"end\": 4038, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 44}, {\"start\": 4135, \"end\": 4192, \"excerpt_start\": 45, \"excerpt_end\": 102}, {\"start\": 4305, \"end\": 5804, \"excerpt_start\": 103, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program\\nLeft Sidebar\\n2 min read · May 16, 2025\\nMay 16, 2025\\nShare\\nWhat is precision hematology?\\nPrecision hematology is an integrated approach to diagnosing and treating blood disorders—particularly hematologic malignancies—by leveraging detailed molecular, genetic, and functional information about each patient’s disease.\\nIt matches therapies more precisely to individual patients by uniting innovative clinical trial designs with cutting-edge diagnostics, such as:\\nAdvanced imaging\\nGenetic profiling\\nDrug-sensitivity testing\\nThis field brings together physicians, scientists, and other key stakeholders across preclinical, translational, and clinical research. Through this collaboration, precision hematology aims to:\\nAccelerate the discovery of new treatment strategies\\nRefine therapeutic decision-making\\nImprove outcomes for patients with blood cancers\\nOur program’s goals\\nOur Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program is designed to promote innovative concepts for diagnostics and innovative clinical trial designs which will feed into the clinical application of precision hematology.\\nThe goal of the program is to create a European regulatory framework for precision hematology. By increasing awareness and providing education, guidelines, and policies, we can improve access to:\\nDiagnostics\\nClinical research\\nTreatment in malignant hematology\\nUseful materials\\nEHA Position Paper on Personalized Treatment for Hematologic Diseases\\nPrecision Medicine in Hematology in 2021: Definitions, Tools, Perspectives, and Open Questions\\nIn Vitro Diagnostic Medical\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-4a63fc37665d223b724eb647\", \"title\": \"Research & Innovation - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Research & Innovation - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3902, \"end\": 4532, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 630}, {\"start\": 4773, \"end\": 4793, \"excerpt_start\": 631, \"excerpt_end\": 651}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Research & Innovation\\nSpecialized Working Groups\\nHemaSphere\\nGrants\\nTopics-in-Focus program\\n“We’ve always recognized the importance of exchanging research ideas. There is a lot of cross-country collaboration, both within Europe and more globally.”\\nDr Sue Pavord, President of the British Society for Hematology\\nOxford University Hospitals NIS FT, United Kingdom\\n“We’ve always recognized the importance of exchanging research ideas. There is a lot of cross-country collaboration, both within Europe and more globally.”\\nDr Sue Pavord, President of the British Society for Hematology\\nOxford University Hospitals NIS FT, United Kingdom\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\